{
  "id": "fim",
  "term": "FIM",
  "definition": "FIM stands for the Family Investment Model, a developmental framework proposing that household income affects children’s outcomes through the resources families invest in them. In this packet, it refers especially to material investments such as spending on education, and also considers relational investments such as parent–child communication.",
